{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"git rev-parse 095ca93f1c33fa71c4e9cc215007b816b4afe028:docs/rubrics/plan-decomposition.md; git show 095ca93f1c33fa71c4e9cc215007b816b4afe028:docs/requirements/stakeholder-needs.toml | Select-String '\"'^'\"\\\\[need.SN-006\\\\]|\"'^'\"\\\\[need.SN-025\\\\]' -Context 0,8\"","aggregated_output":"4f183eb6aa17a459c9b0741391791d03a8f76293\n\r\n> [need.SN-006]\r\n  status = \"Approved\"\r\n  stakeholder_refs = [\"STK-01\"]\r\n  tags = [\"unattended\", \"loop\", \"scripts\", \"personal-data\"]\r\n  need = \"\"\"An agent can run **unattended** and resume from repository text alone. Such a run never waits for \r\ninteractive input, and reports its failures clearly. It also stays **safe**: declared limits bound the workers it may \r\nset running and the actions it takes that cannot be undone, and only an override a human provides — never one the \r\nmodel can set — may relax those limits. That safety is **supervision rather than an absolute**: the layer's first \r\nobligation is to move forward as far as it can, and it surfaces to a human when it cannot proceed — so a fault in the \r\nmachinery that carries a limit degrades to a recorded condition, not to a stopped run.\"\"\"\r\n  why = \"\"\"Agents develop here, and a walk-away run is only worth having if it can be both left alone and trusted \r\nwhile unwatched. The safety half is stated in the need itself rather than only here, because a `why` cell is context \r\nthat nothing derives from: a safety obligation recorded only here leaves the gate enforcing it parentless, and drops \r\nout of any re-derivation of the need.\"\"\"\r\n  priority = \"S\"\r\n  acceptance = \"\"\"The unattended loop resumes from the repository's tracked status surface, exits a **typed code** at \r\neach end state, and a preflight refuses a broken footing (no agent CLI, not a git repo, private author under \r\nprivacy-check) rather than hanging. During unattended operation, configured limits bound every spawned worker and \r\nirreversible action, and only an explicit human-provided override may exceed those limits. A fault in a limit's own \r\nenforcement is recorded and lets the run continue rather than halting it — the run surfaces to a human when it cannot \r\nproceed, never when its own supervision errs.\"\"\"\r\n  \r\n> [need.SN-025]\r\n  status = \"Approved\"\r\n  stakeholder_refs = [\"STK-01\"]\r\n  tags = [\"unattended\", \"loop\"]\r\n  need =\"\"\"**With no human curating what comes next**, a configured LLM agent implements toward the vision — fully \r\nautonomously where enabled — deriving its own next work from the repository's tracked state. (The launcher that starts \r\nit is SN-034's obligation; this need is the self-direction.)\"\"\"\r\n  why = \"\"\"Walk-away autonomy is the whole promise of the unattended layer: if a human must hand-maintain a next-step \r\npointer, the loop is attended in practice and the pointer rots against the registry it paraphrases. Extends SN-006 (a \r\n*resumable* unattended run) into a *self-directing* one.\"\"\"\r\n  priority = \"S\"\r\n  acceptance = \"\"\"A plain launch derives what to do next from the tracked WI DAG plus Git — never from prose or a \r\nhand-maintained pointer, and never from predefined tracks; the ready frontier is ordered deterministically, so two \r\nreaders of the same registry dispatch the same work; the status surface a human reads is generated from that tracked \r\nstate, never hand-copied.\"\"\"\r\n  \r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
